    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I consider math a tool rather than a passion. It's precise and logical, which appeals to me, especially in chemistry and physics. I've always found it practical, not requiring creative flair. I don’t see it as beautiful or elegant, but useful. I enjoy using it for problem-solving, but I don’t engage with it for fun or aesthetic reasons.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. I don’t have a fear of math, and I don’t get anxious about it. I think it's more about efficiency than emotion. When I'm stuck, I take a break, and usually the next day I get a better perspective. My low neuroticism helps; I don’t spiral easily. Math is a process, and I enjoy the journey, even if it's slow.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used a calculator app that explains steps in math problems. It’s been helpful for checking my work and understanding why certain steps are taken. I appreciate how it breaks down complex problems. The experience was smooth and reassuring for me. It didn’t replace my thinking, just clarified my thinking.",
