    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize instruction. They could adapt explanations based on student difficulty and learning style. They could provide instant feedback on problem-solving, helping students understand where they went wrong. They could also generate practice problems and explain concepts in different ways, making math more accessible and less intimidating for all students."
